 "callout": "<b>Why this sits alongside the GA4 dashboard.</b> GA4 only fires for bookings made on our own website widget, so it is blind to <b>OpenTable</b>, only partly captures <b>Google Reserve</b>, and never sees walk-ins or reception and host desks. That is why the two numbers diverge: GA4 reads <b>▼7.5% YoY</b> on website bookings while total covers created across every channel are well ahead of last year. The clearest driver is <b>OpenTable</b>, which was negligible a year ago and is now a material channel across the portfolio, entirely invisible to GA4. Read covers as the fuller demand and channel picture, not as a contradiction of the GA4 story."
